# This file is published AS `.gitignore` in the public snapshot (tools/publish.json
# file_overrides). It is not this repo's own ignore list — that is `.gitignore` at the root, and
# publish.py refuses to run unless every rule there also appears here.
#
# WHY THE TWO DIFFER. A consumer's clone of the snapshot is a deployment, not a development
# monorepo. It grows things this repo either tracks or keeps somewhere else entirely: a `data/`
# directory holding the auth DB and rail corpora, model weights under
# `services/broker/media-assets/`, agent files a coding assistant writes at the root, and the
# rail source material an operator drops in to be indexed. None of that is ignorable here —
# `CLAUDE.md` is a tracked file in the private repo — so inheriting this repo's list verbatim
# left a downstream clone one `git add -A` away from committing SME documents to a PUBLIC remote,
# plus >100 MB weight files GitHub would reject outright.

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Env / secrets
.env
*.local
CLAUDE.local.md.pre-gates
deploy/workstation-keys/
deploy/*.log
deploy/logs/
/var/

# tools/rail_extractability.py scratch snapshots (it cleans up, but not on a crash)
tools/.extract-test/

# Node / web
node_modules/
dist/
.vite/

# OS / editor
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp

# --- public-snapshot additions (not in this repo's own .gitignore) ---------------------------

# Runtime state of a deployed platform: the gateway auth DB, rail corpora, the co-worker inbox.
# Real user data, and it appears the first time the stack runs.
data/

# Any log, anywhere. The private repo only needed deploy/*.log because that is the only place it
# writes them; an install writes them wherever it was run from.
*.log

# Model weights fetched at install time (Kokoro, ONNX embedders). Hundreds of MB, individually
# over GitHub's 100 MB hard limit, so committing them makes the clone unpushable as well as fat.
services/broker/media-assets/

# Coding-assistant files. CLAUDE.md is TRACKED in the private repo (it is the agent guide), which
# is precisely why this list cannot be the same file — everything below it is shared with the
# private list, CLAUDE.md alone is public-only.
CLAUDE.md
CLAUDE.local.md
AGENTS.md
GEMINI.md
.claude/
.cursor/
.aider*
.github/copilot-instructions.md

# Operator-supplied source material for the SME rails. The rail indexes whatever is dropped here;
# it is the operator's own material and must never reach a public remote.
rails/smb-partner-enablement/research/
rails/smb-partner-enablement/documents/
rails/smb-partner-enablement/build/
rails/gemini-cx/research/
rails/gemini-cx/documents/

# Named remote brokers a role may be delegated to (broker upstreams registry). Each entry holds
# that remote's BEARER TOKEN, so this is local configuration and is never committed. The shape is
# in services/broker/upstreams.example.json. Hot-read, like roles.json.
services/broker/upstreams.json
